<summary>Official patch notes</summary>
<p class="mw-empty-elt"></p>
<blockquote class="blizztext" style="border-left: 4px solid #4f545c; padding-left: 10px; margin-left: 0;">
<p>DISCLAIMER: These notes are for addon authors and as such are focused specifically on addon-facing API and security changes only. Changes planned for other parts of the game (UI or otherwise) are not included here.
</p>
</blockquote>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="2026-09-03">2026-09-03</span></h3>
<p><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://discord.com/channels/327414731654692866/1545113129736871966"><font color="yellowgreen"><big><i>Midnight 12.1.5 PTR Changes 1</i></big></font></a> (Build 69594)
</p><summary><span style="color:#ecbc2a"><big>Coming in 12.1.5 PTR 1</big></span></summary>
<p class="mw-empty-elt"></p><p><span style="color: var(--theme-text-color);"><b>Aura Pandemic Animations</b></span><br>
</p>
<ul><li><a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/INTRINSIC_AuraButton" title="INTRINSIC AuraButton">CustomAuraButton</a> now supports Pandemic-triggered animations via new APIs.
<ul><li>Three Pandemic triggers are supported: <b>Enter</b> and <b>Active</b> (both triggered when entering Pandemic), and <b>Leave</b> (triggered when leaving Pandemic).
<ul><li><b>Enter</b> is intended for one-shot animations, while Active is intended for looping animations.</li></ul></li>
<li>Each trigger type has a set of APIs for adding and removing individual animation groups, or clearing all animation groups for that trigger.</li>
<li>Two new <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Secret_Values#Forbidden_aspects" title="Secret Values">forbidden aspects</a> were added to support this:
<ul><li><code>QueryAnimationProgress</code>: prevents querying the progress of an animation or whether it is running.</li>
<li><code>AddAnimations</code>: prevents animations from being added or reparented.</li></ul></li>
<li>Animations used by Pandemic triggers also gain the existing <code>ChangeAnimationTarget</code> forbidden aspect.</li></ul></li></ul>
<div class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-lua mw-content-ltr mw-highlight-copy mw-highlight-copy--bound" dir="ltr"><pre><span></span><span class="kd">local</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nv">glow</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nv">auraButton</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="nf">CreateTexture</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="kc">nil</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="s2">"OVERLAY"</span><span class="p">);</span>
<span class="nv">glow</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="nf">SetColorTexture</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="p">,</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="p">);</span>
<span class="nv">glow</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="nf">SetAllPoints</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nv">auraButton</span><span class="p">);</span>

<span class="kd">local</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nv">animGroup</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nv">glow</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="nf">CreateAnimationGroup</span><span class="p">();</span>
<span class="nv">animGroup</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="nf">SetLooping</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s2">"BOUNCE"</span><span class="p">);</span>

<span class="kd">local</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nv">animAlpha</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="o">=</span><span class="w"> </span><span class="nv">animGroup</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="nf">CreateAnimation</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="s2">"Alpha"</span><span class="p">);</span>
<span class="nv">animAlpha</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="nf">SetFromAlpha</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">0</span><span class="p">);</span>
<span class="nv">animAlpha</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="nf">SetToAlpha</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mi">1</span><span class="p">);</span>
<span class="nv">animAlpha</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="nf">SetDuration</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="mf">0.5</span><span class="p">);</span>

<span class="nv">auraButton</span><span class="p">:</span><span class="nf">AddPandemicActiveAnimation</span><span class="p">(</span><span class="nv">animGroup</span><span class="p">);</span>
</pre><button type="button">Copy</button></div>
<p><span style="color: var(--theme-text-color);"><b>Aura Containers</b></span><br>
</p>
<ul><li><code>CustomAuraButton</code> now supports showing the aura's caster in a fontstring via the new <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:AuraButton_SetCasterName" title="API:AuraButton SetCasterName">SetCasterName</a> API.</li>
<li><a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:AuraButton_AddDispelTypeTexture" title="API:AuraButton AddDispelTypeTexture">AddDispelTypeTexture</a> and <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:AuraButton_AddPandemicRegion" title="API:AuraButton AddPandemicRegion">AddPandemicRegion</a> no longer return an index. The corresponding <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:AuraButton_RemoveDispelTypeTexture" title="API:AuraButton RemoveDispelTypeTexture">RemoveDispelTypeTexture</a> and <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:AuraButton_RemovePandemicRegion" title="API:AuraButton RemovePandemicRegion">RemovePandemicRegion</a> APIs now take a region reference instead of an index.</li>
<li><code>AddDispelTypeTexture</code> and <code>AddPandemicRegion</code> now raise an error if the same region is added multiple times.</li>
<li>Aura tooltips now support displaying the aura's caster, colorized by reaction or class color. This functionality is controlled by the new <span class="tttemplatelink"><span class="redlink-removed" title="null"><span style="color: var(--wowapi-text-color-alt);">tooltipShowAuraCasterNames</span></span></span><span style="display:none">CVar: <font color="#71d5ff">tooltipShowAuraCasterNames</font> (Game)<br>Default: <code><span class="apitype">0</span></code>, Scope: <span class="apitype">Account</span><br><small>Show caster unit names in tooltips for unit auras.</small></span> CVar.</li>
<li>New <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/INTRINSIC_AuraContainer" title="INTRINSIC AuraContainer">CustomAuraContainer</a> APIs allow individual items to be <b>disabled</b> via <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:AuraContainer_SetAuraGroupEnabled" title="API:AuraContainer SetAuraGroupEnabled">SetAuraGroupEnabled</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:AuraContainer_SetAuraSlotEnabled" title="API:AuraContainer SetAuraSlotEnabled">SetAuraSlotEnabled</a>, and <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:AuraContainer_SetItemEnchantmentEnabled" title="API:AuraContainer SetItemEnchantmentEnabled">SetItemEnchantmentEnabled</a>.</li>
<li><code>CustomAuraButton</code> now supports a <code>minApplications</code> option in <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:AuraButton_SetApplicationBar" title="API:AuraButton SetApplicationBar">SetApplicationBar</a>, which prevents the application bar from being shown unless the number of applications exceeds the specified value.</li>
<li>A new <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:AuraContainer_SetEditModePreviewEnabled" title="API:AuraContainer SetEditModePreviewEnabled">SetEditModePreviewEnabled</a> API has been added to <code>CustomAuraContainer</code> to control whether preview auras are shown while the player is in Edit Mode.</li>
<li><code>CustomAuraContainer</code> now correctly refreshes in response to <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Event:UNIT_FLAGS" title="Event:UNIT FLAGS">UNIT_FLAGS</a> and <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Event:UNIT_FACTION" title="Event:UNIT FACTION">UNIT_FACTION</a> events.</li></ul>
<p><span style="color: var(--theme-text-color);"><b>AddOn Security</b></span><br>
</p>
<ul><li>The <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:Cooldown_SetCooldown" title="API:Cooldown SetCooldown">SetCooldown</a> and <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:Cooldown_Clear" title="API:Cooldown Clear">Clear</a> cooldown APIs can no longer be called from tainted code when the cooldown frame itself is protected.</li>
<li>Castbar IDs are now <b>unique per unit token</b>, preventing addons from using them to compare units.
<ul><li><b>Note:</b> Unit token casing matters when querying castbar IDs; a <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:UnitCastingInfo" title="API:UnitCastingInfo">UnitCastingInfo</a> query for <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-lua mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr"><span class="s2">"PLAYER"</span></code> returns a different castbar ID than one for <code class="mw-highlight mw-highlight-lang-lua mw-content-ltr" dir="ltr"><span class="s2">"player"</span></code>. Events always use <b>lowercase unit tokens</b>.</li></ul></li></ul>
<p><span style="color: var(--theme-text-color);"><b>Script Object APIs</b></span><br>
</p>
<ul><li>A new <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/ScriptObject_TimedSignalMap" title="ScriptObject TimedSignalMap">TimedSignalMap</a> script object has been added for scheduling a <b>single callback</b> which is invoked with <b>user-defined keys</b> at specified times.
<ul><li>Keys can be dynamically <b>rescheduled without requiring cancellation</b>, unlike timer objects, making <code>TimedSignalMap</code> useful as a lower-level scheduling primitive.</li>
<li>The <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://www.townlong-yak.com/framexml/ptr/go/TimerUtil.CreateTimedSignalCallbackMap">CreateTimedSignalCallbackMap</a> API (in <code>TimerUtil</code>) is a convenience wrapper that generates keys and associates each key with a callback.</li></ul></li>
<li>A new <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:CreateFrameWithOptions" title="API:CreateFrameWithOptions">CreateFrameWithOptions</a> API has been added, which takes a table with named options as its only parameter.
<ul><li>The options currently supported mirror those accepted by <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:CreateFrame" title="API:CreateFrame">CreateFrame</a>: <code>frameType</code> (required), <code>name</code>, <code>parent</code>, <code>inherits</code> (as an <i>array</i> of template names), <code>id</code>, and <code>hidden</code> (new; hides the frame by default).</li></ul></li>
<li>Added a new <code>roundLayoutToNearestPixel</code> XML attribute and <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:ScriptRegion_SetRoundLayoutToNearestPixel" title="API:ScriptRegion SetRoundLayoutToNearestPixel">SetRoundLayoutToNearestPixel</a> API to all Regions. When enabled, layout changes are automatically <b>rounded to the nearest pixel</b>.
<ul><li>These provide a <b>native-code replacement</b> for the Lua <code>PixelUtil</code> functions; <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://www.townlong-yak.com/framexml/ptr/go/PixelUtil.SetRoundLayoutToNearestPixelRecursively">PixelUtil.SetRoundLayoutToNearestPixelRecursively</a> can be used to apply the setting to a region and all its children.</li></ul></li></ul>
<p><span style="color: var(--theme-text-color);"><b>Lua Utility Functions</b></span><br>
</p>
<ul><li>A suite of math, string, and table utility functions has been added. Some were previously implemented in Lua and have now been moved to native code; aliases for the existing names have been retained to prevent addon breakage.
<ul><li>Math functions: <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:math.clamp" title="API:math.clamp">math.clamp</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:math.saturate" title="API:math.saturate">math.saturate</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:math.round" title="API:math.round">math.round</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:math.lerp" title="API:math.lerp">math.lerp</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:math.normalize" title="API:math.normalize">math.normalize</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:math.sign" title="API:math.sign">math.sign</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:math.remap" title="API:math.remap">math.remap</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:math.wrap" title="API:math.wrap">math.wrap</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:math.isfinite" title="API:math.isfinite">math.isfinite</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:math.isnan" title="API:math.isnan">math.isnan</a>, and <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:math.isinf" title="API:math.isinf">math.isinf</a>.</li>
<li>String functions: <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:string.contains" title="API:string.contains">string.contains</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:string.ltrim" title="API:string.ltrim">string.ltrim</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:string.rtrim" title="API:string.rtrim">string.rtrim</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:string.startswith" title="API:string.startswith">string.startswith</a>, and <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:string.endswith" title="API:string.endswith">string.endswith</a>.</li>
<li>Table functions: <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:table.isempty" title="API:table.isempty">table.isempty</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:table.contains" title="API:table.contains">table.contains</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:table.indexof" title="API:table.indexof">table.indexof</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:table.removeunordered" title="API:table.removeunordered">table.removeunordered</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:table.removevalue" title="API:table.removevalue">table.removevalue</a>, <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:table.keys" title="API:table.keys">table.keys</a>, and <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:table.values" title="API:table.values">table.values</a>.</li></ul></li></ul>
<p><span style="color: var(--theme-text-color);"><b>Deprecations</b></span><br>
</p>
<ul><li>The following deprecated addons have been removed. Update your code to no longer use the deprecated APIs they contained:
<ul><li><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.0/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_DeprecatedCurrencyScript/Deprecated_CurrencyScript.lua">Blizzard_DeprecatedCurrencyScript</a></li>
<li><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.0/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_DeprecatedGlue/Deprecated_Glue.lua">Blizzard_DeprecatedGlue</a></li>
<li><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.0/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_DeprecatedItemScript/Deprecated_ItemScript.lua">Blizzard_DeprecatedItemScript</a></li>
<li><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.0/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_DeprecatedItemSocketInfo/Deprecated_ItemSocketInfo.lua">Blizzard_DeprecatedItemSocketInfo</a></li>
<li><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.0/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_DeprecatedLFG/Deprecated_LFG.lua">Blizzard_DeprecatedLFG</a></li>
<li><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.0/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_DeprecatedPetInfo/Deprecated_PetInfo.lua">Blizzard_DeprecatedPetInfo</a></li>
<li><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.0/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_DeprecatedPvpScript/Deprecated_PvpScript.lua">Blizzard_DeprecatedPvpScript</a></li>
<li><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.0/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_DeprecatedSoundScript/Deprecated_SoundScript.lua">Blizzard_DeprecatedSoundScript</a></li>
<li><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.0/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_DeprecatedTradeInfo/Deprecated_TradeInfo.lua">Blizzard_DeprecatedTradeInfo</a></li>
<li><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.0/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_DeprecatedWorldElapsedTimerTypes/Deprecated_WorldElapsedTimerTypes.lua">Blizzard_DeprecatedWorldElapsedTimerTypes</a></li></ul></li></ul>
<p><span style="color: var(--theme-text-color);"><b>Miscellaneous</b></span><br>
</p>
<ul><li>A new <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Category:API_systems/WeatherScript" title="Category:API systems/WeatherScript">C_Weather</a> namespace blows in, providing access to current weather conditions and an event when they change.</li>
<li>A new <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Category:API_systems/Intl" title="Category:API systems/Intl">C_Intl</a> namespace provides functions for working with Unicode and internationalization.</li>
<li>The spell ID line shown in spell tooltips via the <span class="tttemplatelink"><span class="redlink-removed" title="null"><span style="color: var(--wowapi-text-color-alt);">tooltipShowAuraSpellIDs</span></span></span><span style="display:none">CVar: <font color="#71d5ff">tooltipShowAuraSpellIDs</font> (Game)<br>Default: <code><span class="apitype">0</span></code><br><small>Show spell IDs in tooltips for unit auras.</small></span> CVar is now correctly localized, and no longer uses the same color as spell description text.</li>
<li>Mythic+ enemy forces lines in tooltips now use a distinct line type: <code>Enum.TooltipDataLineType.UnitCriteriaProgress</code>.</li>
<li>Pinging a macro containing a <code>#showtooltip</code> line now pings the corresponding spell.</li>
<li>Fixed an issue that could prevent duration objects from rendering for long-duration auras in some cases.</li>
<li>Fixed a performance issue with the <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:EnumerateFrames" title="API:EnumerateFrames">EnumerateFrames</a> API.</li>
<li>Fixed an issue where calling <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:Frame_Hide" title="API:Frame Hide">Hide</a> directly on a panel, rather than <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://www.townlong-yak.com/framexml/ptr/go/HideUIPanel">HideUIPanel</a>, could prevent the Game Menu from being shown.</li></ul>
<hr>
<p><br>
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="2026-09-16">2026-09-16</span></h3>
<p><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://discord.com/channels/327414731654692866/1549542072816635984"><font color="yellowgreen"><big><i>Midnight 12.1.5 PTR Changes 2</i></big></font></a> (Build 69848)
</p><summary><span style="color:#ecbc2a"><big>Coming in 12.1.5 PTR 2</big></span></summary>
<p class="mw-empty-elt"></p><p><span style="color: var(--theme-text-color);"><b>Aura Containers</b></span><br>
</p>
<ul><li>Fixed an issue where using <code>includeSpellIDs</code> to show only specific never-secret auras, such as Sated, could also allow unrelated auras through.</li>
<li>Fixed an issue where the <code>ProcessAura</code> policy did not correctly filter out auras that returned <code>ProcessAuraType.None</code>.</li>
<li><a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/INTRINSIC_AuraButton" title="INTRINSIC AuraButton">CustomAuraButton</a> now supports two additional animation triggers.
<ul><li><b>Shown</b> animations play the first time an aura becomes visible on the button, and stop when the aura is no longer shown, using <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://www.townlong-yak.com/framexml/ptr/go/CustomAuraButtonSharedMixin:AddAuraShownAnimation">AddAuraShownAnimation</a>.</li>
<li><b>Assigned</b> animations play whenever a new aura is assigned to the button, independent of visibility, using <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://www.townlong-yak.com/framexml/ptr/go/CustomAuraButtonSharedMixin:AddAuraAssignedAnimation">AddAuraAssignedAnimation</a>.</li></ul></li>
<li><code>CustomAuraButton</code> animations now apply <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Secret_aspects" class="mw-redirect" title="Secret aspects">secret aspects</a> for <code>VertexColor</code> and <code>TexCoords</code> to target objects.</li></ul>
<p><span style="color: var(--theme-text-color);"><b>AddOn Security</b></span><br>
</p>
<ul><li>The <code>sourceGUID</code> field returned by Damage Meter APIs is now secret when the unit's identity is secret.</li>
<li>Added a new <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.5/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_UnitFrame/Shared/UnitFrameUtil.lua">UnitFrameUtil</a> Lua library, focused on providing addon-safe APIs for unit frame addons to set textures based on now-secret APIs.
<ul><li>The first new API is <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.5/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_UnitFrame/Shared/UnitFrameUtil.lua#L145">UpdateUnitPvPIndicator</a>, with more APIs coming in future PTR builds.</li></ul></li>
<li><a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/C_Intl" class="mw-redirect" title="C Intl">C_Intl</a> functions now accept <b>secret string arguments from tainted code</b>.
<ul><li>The <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:C_Intl.Transliterate" title="API:C Intl.Transliterate">C_Intl.Transliterate</a> API does not allow <code>Null</code> or <code>Remove</code> transliterators for secret text from tainted code.</li></ul></li>
<li>The <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:C_Intl.FindStringMatches" title="API:C Intl.FindStringMatches">C_Intl.FindStringMatches</a> and <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:C_Intl.FindBreaks" title="API:C Intl.FindBreaks">C_Intl.FindBreaks</a> APIs now return <b>1-based indices</b>.</li>
<li>Fixed a bug where RaidWarning frames could retain secret aspects on their fontstrings after being returned to the pool.</li>
<li>Addons now get an <b>additional one-frame window</b> to adjust the hitbox of an enemy nameplate if a <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Event:UNIT_CLASSIFICATION_CHANGED" title="Event:UNIT CLASSIFICATION CHANGED">UNIT_CLASSIFICATION_CHANGED</a> event arrives after the nameplate was already created.</li></ul>
<p><span style="color: var(--theme-text-color);"><b>Miscellaneous</b></span><br>
</p>
<ul><li>A new optional <code>throttleSeconds</code> parameter was added to the <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:C_UnitAuras.AddAuraSound" title="API:C UnitAuras.AddAuraSound">C_UnitAuras.AddAuraSound</a> API, allowing addons to specify <b>how often the sound should be allowed to play</b>.</li>
<li>Fixed an issue that could cause some APIs, like tostring and dumpobject, to crash when passed secret objects.</li>
<li>Chat tabs no longer use <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://www.townlong-yak.com/framexml/ptr/go/UIFrameFlash">UIFrameFlash</a> for their flash animations, hopefully <b>reducing chat tab taint issues</b> caused by unrelated systems.</li>
<li><a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:C_ClassColor.GetClassColor" title="API:C ClassColor.GetClassColor">C_ClassColor.GetClassColor</a> now accepts an <b>optional tint color</b>, which is multiplied by the class color before it is returned.</li>
<li><a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:GetPlayerInfoByGUID" title="API:GetPlayerInfoByGUID">GetPlayerInfoByGUID</a> now also returns the unit's level, if known.</li>
<li>The following CVars, removed in Midnight, have been restored: <span class="tttemplatelink"><span class="redlink-removed" title="null"><span style="color: var(--wowapi-text-color-alt);">nameplateMotionSpeed</span></span></span><span style="display:none">CVar: <font color="#71d5ff">nameplateMotionSpeed</font> (Game)<br>Default: <code><span class="apitype">0.025000</span></code><br><small>Controls the rate at which nameplate animates into their target locations [0.0-1.0]</small></span>, <span class="tttemplatelink"><span class="redlink-removed" title="null"><span style="color: var(--wowapi-text-color-alt);">nameplateBottomInset</span></span></span><span style="display:none">CVar: <font color="#71d5ff">nameplateBottomInset</font> (Game)<br>Default: <code><span class="apitype">0.100000</span></code><br><small>The inset from the bottom (in screen percent) that nameplates are clamped to.</small></span>, and <span class="tttemplatelink"><span class="redlink-removed" title="null"><span style="color: var(--wowapi-text-color-alt);">nameplateTopInset</span></span></span><span style="display:none">CVar: <font color="#71d5ff">nameplateTopInset</font> (Game)<br>Default: <code><span class="apitype">0.080000</span></code><br><small>The inset from the top (in screen percent) that nameplates are clamped to.</small></span>.</li>
<li><a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/UIOBJECT_RadialProgress" title="UIOBJECT RadialProgress">RadialProgress</a> animations can now be created from XML.</li>
<li>Fixed a texture masking bug affecting frames using more than one mask texture with different wrap modes.</li>
<li>Fixed a bug that could cause the right-click unit menu to incorrectly show battle-pet options for a distant player. This is <b>pending a hotfix to 12.1.0</b> as well.</li></ul>
<hr>
<p><br>
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="2026-09-22">2026-09-22</span></h3>
<p><a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://discord.com/channels/327414731654692866/1552068745374081104"><font color="yellowgreen"><big><i>Midnight 12.1.5 PTR Changes 3</i></big></font></a> (Build 69952)
</p><summary><span style="color:#ecbc2a"><big>Coming in 12.1.5 PTR 3</big></span></summary>
<p class="mw-empty-elt"></p><p><span style="color: var(--theme-text-color);"><b>Addon Security</b></span><br>
</p>
<ul><li>The <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:GetArenaOpponentSpec" title="API:GetArenaOpponentSpec">GetArenaOpponentSpec</a> API now returns secrets.</li>
<li><code>UnitFrameUtil</code> library introduced in the last PTR build has been expanded with APIs for raid role icons and arena opponent specs. It has also been moved to shared code, making it available in Classic.
<ul><li>New APIs <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.5/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_UnitFrame/Shared/UnitFrameUtil.lua#L343">GetArenaOpponentSpecDisplayInfo</a>, <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.5/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_UnitFrame/Shared/UnitFrameUtil.lua#L357">UpdateArenaOpponentSpecDisplay</a>, and <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.5/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_UnitFrame/Shared/UnitFrameUtil.lua#L406">UpdateArenaOpponentSpecDisplayName</a> give addons secret-safe access to an arena opponent's spec name, class name, spec icon, role icon, and class-color bar tint.</li>
<li>New APIs <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.5/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_UnitFrame/Shared/UnitFrameUtil.lua#L248">GetUnitRoleIconDisplayInfo</a> and <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://github.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/blob/12.1.5/Interface/AddOns/Blizzard_UnitFrame/Shared/UnitFrameUtil.lua#L262">UpdateUnitFrameRoleIcon</a> let addons set up raid role icons (including vehicle and main tank/assist icons) for raid members even when their identities are secret.</li>
<li>All <code>UnitFrameUtil</code> display APIs now accept an optional <code>textureMap</code> table so addons can override the default textures/atlases used.</li></ul></li>
<li>Added <a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/API:C_UnitAuras.GetRefreshCarryOverDuration" title="API:C UnitAuras.GetRefreshCarryOverDuration">C_UnitAuras.GetRefreshCarryOverDuration</a>, a secret-aware API returning how much of an aura's remaining duration would carry over on refresh. <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://www.townlong-yak.com/framexml/ptr/go/AuraContainerUtil.GetPandemicWindow">AuraContainerUtil.GetPandemicWindow</a> now uses this internally, fixing incorrect pandemic-window timing for auras that can extend past the normal refresh cap (e.g. <span class="nobreak"><span class="linkicon"><img alt="" src="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/images/thumb/Inv_misc_herb_felblossom.png/16px-Inv_misc_herb_felblossom.png?b83774" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="16" height="16" data-file-width="64" data-file-height="64"> </span><a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Lifebloom"><span class="abilitylink ajaxttlink"><span class="bracket">[</span>Lifebloom<span class="bracket">]</span></span></a></span> + <span class="nobreak"><span class="linkicon"><img alt="" src="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/images/thumb/Spell_nature_tranquility.png/16px-Spell_nature_tranquility.png?f85d20" decoding="async" loading="lazy" width="16" height="16" data-file-width="64" data-file-height="64"> </span><a href="https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Tranquility"><span class="abilitylink ajaxttlink"><span class="bracket">[</span>Tranquility<span class="bracket">]</span></span></a></span>).</li></ul>
<hr>
<p><br>
</p>
